Breakeven trades and the order of trades
A trade that closes at zero, usually because the stop was moved to the entry price, is neither a win nor a loss. Build() leaves it out by default. It can also count it as a loss or as a win, since some people see a breakeven exit as a failed trade. The band around zero is half the smallest unit of the deposit currency, 0.005 on a USD account and 0.5 on an account in a currency without decimals. The net of a trade is a sum of several doubles, so it doesn't always land on exactly 0. SetBreakevenEps() sets a wider band for anyone who counts a trade within a few cents as breakeven.
