Leaving breakeven trades out has a side effect. Two trades that were not neighbors in time become neighbors in the sequence, and that can change the run count. In every backtest run in this article the report shows "breakeven 0", so the choice made no difference here. On an EA with many breakeven exits, compare BE_SKIP with BE_AS_LOSS before trusting either.
The order is the close time in milliseconds, from DEAL_TIME_MSC. When two trades close in the same millisecond, the lower position ID comes first, so the order never depends on how the history happens to be listed.
